{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfvb127FobRHdnoxDW72P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Recommendation: don't start the US study now. Fix UK unit economics first.\n\n**Why the study is the wrong first step**\n- **Runway.** A three-month study uses a third of your nine months and produces no revenue. Even if the answer is \"go\", you'd have about six months left to fund a launch you can't yet afford.\n- **Broken economics.** Payback takes 26 months against a 12-month target, so every new customer is currently a net cash drain within your runway. In a new market, acquisition costs are usually higher because you have no brand, referrals or local SEO. Expanding would likely spread the same losses over more customers.\n- **Regulation.** US childcare rules vary by state, so the US is really dozens of separate launches. That adds compliance and legal cost and spreads the team thinner.\n\n**What to do instead (next 3–4 months)**\n1. **Cut payback time.** Shift spend away from your worst-performing acquisition channels, push referrals and retention, and look at pricing, take rate and subscription options. Set monthly milestones, e.g. payback under 18 months by month 3 and heading toward 12.\n2. **Extend runway.** Cut costs, or raise a bridge round now, while you still have time to negotiate.\n3. **Set conditions for revisiting the US.** For example, payback of 12 months or less, at least 18 months of runway, and UK growth that holds up.\n\n**What to offer the board member**\nIf they want progress on the US, propose a two-week desk review with no spend. One person scopes it to one or two states with the simplest rules and estimates US acquisition costs. That keeps the option open without risking the company.\n\nThe point to make to the board: the US can wait until the UK pays for itself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3193,"cache_read_input_tokens":4992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3193},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a76acfd-cc0f-46b0-a3c8-a842806d89a6","uuid":"cec800bf-1534-4cb6-9b3e-e38865bac6a5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:12:56.861Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvb11nAncEzfJjqUZ2vL"}
